# UK date format

The site serves Ireland/UK visitors. Show **Gregorian dates in British/Irish style**: day before month, never US order (`Jun 24, 2026`). **Times:** see `.cursor/rules/uk-time-format.mdc`.

## Allowed formats

| Style | Example | When to use |
|-------|---------|-------------|
| Short | 24 Jun 2026 | Compact UI, week ranges |
| Medium (default) | 24 June 2026 | Nav labels, deck chips |
| Long | Wednesday, 24 June 2026 | Programme events, daily timetable |
| Ordinal | 24th June 2026 | Optional emphasis (`formatUkDate` + `{ ordinal: true }`) |

## JavaScript

Use helpers in `scripts.js` (do not hand-roll or use `en-US`):

- `formatUkDate(date, preset)` — ISO/UTC timestamps → `Europe/Dublin`
- `formatUkDateLocal(date, preset)` — calendar dates already built from Dublin day parts
- `formatGregorianFromRecord(record, preset)` — prayer timetable rows (prefer `gregorianYear/Month/Day` over API `gregorianDateString`)
- `formatUkDisplayDate(string, preset)` — reformat API text that may be US-shaped

Presets: `short`, `medium`, `long`, `weekdayLong`, `weekdayShort`, `monthLong`, etc.

```javascript
// ❌ US order risk
date.toLocaleDateString("en-US", { month: "short", day: "numeric", year: "numeric" });

// ✅ UK
formatUkDate(isoDate, "short");           // 24 Jun 2026
formatUkDateLocal(calendarDate, "medium"); // 24 June 2026
```

## HTML

- Static copy: `24 June 2026`, `March 2024`, not `June 24, 2024`.
- Placeholder values in templates are overwritten by JS; keep them UK-shaped (`Jan` short month is fine in the date chip layout).

## Locale

- Page `lang="en-GB"`; `Intl` locale `en-GB` (or `en-IE` for Ireland date parts).
- Time zone: `Europe/Dublin` for live clocks and ISO timestamps.
